        "model": "campaign_trail.question",
        "pk": 1193,
        "fields": {
            "description": "Osama bin Laden. CIA analysts believe they've located him in a compound in Abbottabad, Pakistan, less than a mile from the country's military academy. We don't have photographic proof, and nobody can tell us with absolute certainty that he's inside, but the intelligence community thinks the odds are good enough that they're putting options in front of you. Pakistan hasn't been informed. If we tell them and bin Laden is there, there's a very real possibility somebody tips him off. If we go in ourselves, we're conducting a military operation inside the territory of a supposed ally without their permission. You're the one making the call. What'll it be, Mr. President? "
        }
