        "model": "campaign_trail.question",
        "pk": 1196,
        "fields": {
            "description": "We're in Denver for the first presidential debate, and Daniels came ready for this one. Asked about the economy, he rattles off the cost of your two recovery packages, the auto rescue and the expansion of federal healthcare before turning directly toward you. “Mr. President, nobody disputes that you inherited a terrible economy. But four years later, millions of Americans are still struggling, we've added enormously to the national debt, and your answer to virtually every problem has been another federal program. At some point, you have to ask whether government is helping the recovery or holding it back.” Jim Lehrer turns to you. You've got two minutes."
        }
